# RUNTIME plus TEST tooling. This file is what the App Store's generated pipeline installs
# before it runs pytest, so it MUST carry the test tooling: the pipeline is generated and
# cannot be edited to add a second file. A runtime-only version of this file failed the
# platform's Test stage with `pytest: command not found`, exit 127, taking Quality, Container
# Build and Container Scan down with it.
#
# The IMAGE installs requirements-runtime.txt, which is lean. Two files, two jobs:
#   requirements-runtime.txt  -> the container image
#   requirements.txt          -> the platform test stage and the local loop
#   requirements-dev.txt      -> local-only lint, type and audit tooling
#
# Policy (dependencies skill): no new runtime dependency without a recorded reason. Each
# reason is below. Exact pins are resolved into the hash-locked lock files by
# scripts/lock-requirements.sh.
#
# fastapi  - boundary validation. Pydantic models reject a malformed body at the edge
#            rather than coercing it, which is the fail-closed rule the security gate
#            checks. Writing that by hand is more code and more risk than the pin.
# uvicorn  - the ASGI server the App Store python recipe's gunicorn worker class needs.
# gunicorn - the process manager in the reference CMD; gives SIGTERM handling and
#            worker supervision the platform expects.
# sgp4     - the propagator the flight plan mandates (MIT), and the ONLY way to score
#            anything: every scenario, drill item and debrief is measured against
#            propagated state. It ships the official Vallado AIAA 2006-6753
#            verification data (SGP4-VER.TLE, tcppver.out), so the golden tests read the
#            published reference output rather than numbers this project invented.
#            Hand-writing SGP4 would be a fabrication risk with no upside.
#
# DEFERRED, with reasons, so the runtime image stays lean until each is genuinely used:
#   numpy    - not needed for propagation or the determinism harness, which are scalar.
#              Add it with the Clohessy-Wiltshire relative-motion work, not before.
#   skyfield - frames and time. Deferred to the frame-conversion step; it pulls an
#              ephemeris dependency and the air-gap posture means any data file it wants
#              has to be vendored deliberately, not discovered at runtime.
fastapi==0.141.1
uvicorn==0.52.3
gunicorn==26.1.0
sgp4==2.24

# TEST tooling. Present here because the platform's generated test stage installs THIS file
# and then runs pytest. Kept to what running the suite needs; the lint, type and audit tools
# stay in requirements-dev.txt because the platform never runs them.
pytest==9.1.1
pytest-cov==7.1.0
coverage==7.15.4
httpx==0.28.1
hypothesis==6.148.4
